# NO NEWSPAPER LANGUAGE IN DOCUMENTATION

## THE RULE

This is technical documentation. Write about what IS, not what "appeared", "is now available", or "has been added".

## FORBIDDEN PATTERNS

```
Wrong: Basic VMs can now be created via the API.
Wrong: A new region_id field has been added.
Wrong: We've added support for PATCH endpoints.
Wrong: This feature is now available.
Wrong: теперь, появилось, добавили, добавлена поддержка
```

## CORRECT PATTERNS

```
Right: Basic VMs use region-less endpoints.
Right: The request body includes region_id.
Right: PATCH accepts name, tags, and interfaces[].
Right: The API returns {"tasks": [...]}.
```

## THE RULE IN ONE SENTENCE

Describe the current state of the feature. Never announce it.
